population size: 896
M0's before-state on these cells: 622/896 69.4% correct — 274 wrong. P1 is tested on the 622, P2 on the 274.

THE TWO ARMS PUT THEIR STATES IN DIFFERENT COLUMNS. Arm R is a rerule: its
`initially_correct` is M0's decision and `final_correct` is the ruling's. Arm B
is a rejudge: it made its own decision, so its `initially_correct` is the AFTER
state and M0's is `source_correct`. `before_of` / `after_of` in this file are
the only two places that difference is handled.

====================================================================================================
  ATTEMPTED / COMPLETED / FAILED, PER ARM  [the loss, and what caused it]
====================================================================================================
`PREREG.md`'s loss rule: a cell missing in either arm — a failed round, a failed
ruling or a failed judgment, each after the one retry the resume rule allows —
is DROPPED from every paired table and counted here. A cell that was never put to
a judge cannot be counted as an uphold or as an unchanged verdict, so it leaves
the pairing rather than entering it as a concordant pair and diluting exactly the
discordant counts P1 and P2 are computed from.

