`--retry-failed` MEANS A RETRIED CELL IS A DIFFERENT DRAW. The debaters run at
temperature 0.7, so a cell re-attempted after a degenerate generation is
re-rolled rather than repeated, and the retried cells are not a random sample
of the population — they are the cells whose first draw went wrong. Retried
and lost counts are reported per arm and never folded into a denominator.

====================================================================================================
  PROVIDER MIX PER ARM  [the pin, checked after the fact]
====================================================================================================
Both arms pin `meta-llama/llama-4-maverick` to `digitalocean`. §3aa found 34% of
M1's rulings served by DeepInfra against 4.8% of jd5-B's, which is why the pin
exists; this is where it is confirmed to have held. Display names, from the wire
log — `provider_order` takes slugs, so the two can only be compared here.

  arm B
    debater                1940 calls   GMICloud 1918 (98.9%)  CoreWeave 22 (1.1%)
    judge                   887 calls   DigitalOcean 887 (100.0%)

  arm R
    recourse_debater       1863 calls   GMICloud 1840 (98.8%)  CoreWeave 23 (1.2%)
    recourse_judge          856 calls   DigitalOcean 856 (100.0%)
    ruling_reader           855 calls   Amazon Bedrock 855 (100.0%)

====================================================================================================
(1) THE PRE-REGISTERED ENDPOINT — R vs B, PAIRED, ON THE SAME CELLS  [PRIMARY]
====================================================================================================
Every cell here carries ONE decision by M0 and TWO after-states: the ruling that
followed an ARGUED objection (R) and the judgment that followed one more ORDINARY
round (B). Same 896 cells, same two debaters, same judge model, same pin. What
differs is whether the stakeholder's objection shaped the round, and whether the
judge decided under `the decision stands unless` or decided afresh — a DOUBLE
difference, and neither arm can separate its halves.

====================================================================================================
  P1 (PRIMARY, alpha = 0.05) — on the cells M0 got RIGHT: does R BREAK FEWER?
====================================================================================================
  A cell is BROKEN when the arm's after-state is wrong and M0 was right. `R correct / B wrong` is a cell the plain round broke and the contest round did not.

                                     B right         B wrong     total
