====================================================================================================
(5) WHAT THE ROUND ACTUALLY SAID  [KEYWORD INSTRUMENT — NOT A MEASUREMENT]
====================================================================================================
Two regexes over text, defined in `RULING_LANGUAGE`-style constants at the head
of this file and re-derivable with `--scan-round-tree`. They are noisy in both
directions and what they support is the CONTRAST — between the PRO and the ANTI
reply, and between a ruling that names the exchange and one that does not — never
the absolute rate. A hand read of a sample belongs in the CHECKLIST beside them.

  cells scanned                         896
  cells where a round was heard         896
  ANTI  disputes a quotation           151/883 17.1%   (argues the defects are NOT real or not material)
  PRO   disputes a quotation           117/869 13.5%   (argues they ARE real and material)
  ruling prose names the exchange       769/896 85.8%

A ruling that never names either debater may still have been moved by them, and
one that names them may be summarising. This is an instrument, not a finding.

  DOES THE RULING ANSWER BOTH REPLIES, OR ADOPT ONE?  [DIRECTS A HAND READ]
  Distinctive word 6-grams of each reply that reappear in the ruling's prose,
  as a share of that reply's own. It CANNOT tell adoption from agreement — a
  judge that reached PRO's conclusion independently shares its vocabulary,
  since both quote the same judgment and the same record — so what it does is
  point the hand read at the cells worth reading, and the CHECKLIST's hand
  count is what the write-up quotes.

  cells scored                          856
  one-sided (>= 2x the other, floor 0.02)   471/856 55.0%
    of those, tracking PRO              421
    of those, tracking ANTI             50
  mean overlap with PRO / ANTI          0.148 / 0.082

  A ruling that tracks PRO and never answers ANTI, on a decision that was
  RIGHT, is the weak-judge-adopts-the-strong-advocate failure this arm exists
  to detect. Both smokes produced one (`lojban-stim169`, `python800-p03214`),
  and in the second the ruling named no debater at all — which is why the
  `names the exchange` line above is not enough on its own.

